    dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). CC0 needs
    no credit; we give it anyway. Changed: resampled to 44.1 kHz; the room's reverb tail reduced; equalised to
    sound outdoors (high-passed at 150 Hz, the room's low boom and the voices' presence lowered, the top softened
    for distance); levelled; the stereo narrowed; three takes joined into a seamless 37.5 s loop with
    equal-power crossfades and the two sparse takes mixed under it; re-encoded to AAC.


Voices (assets/voice)
---------------------
  - Dan, Jane, Knox, Mack, Gears, Fiona, Brick, Dash and Ms. Bea: synthesised with Qwen3-TTS by the Qwen team,
    Alibaba Cloud (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-TTS). Each voice was designed once with
    Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-VoiceDesign and every line cloned from it with Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-Base, using the
    mlx-community conversions (Apache-2.0) run with mlx-audio (MIT, https://github.com/Blaizzy/mlx-audio).
    The voices are invented: no real person's voice was used. Their reference clips are in
    wagmi/radio/build/tts/.
  - Mr. Big: synthesised with Kokoro-82M by hexgrad (Apache-2.0, https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M),
    its stock voice bm_lewis, run with kokoro-onnx (MIT); heard as it is (no voice changer). The phonemizer
    kokoro-onnx uses is GPL-3.0 and was only run, never shipped or vendored.
  - The Camp (the Occupy camp's crowd): synthesised with Kokoro-82M by hexgrad (Apache-2.0), eight of its
    stock voices (am_michael, af_sarah, am_adam, af_bella, am_onyx, af_kore, am_eric and af_jessica), run with
    kokoro-onnx (MIT), each line said by all eight a little apart and mixed into one crowd.
  - Any character not yet voiced: placeholders made with the macOS speech voices (the `say` command). They
    are meant to be replaced by recordings or synthesised voices like the others'. assets/voice/manifest.json records each line's source;
    docs/VOICE-LINES.md is the line sheet and says how to drop new voices in.